<title>ESTONIA: NORDIKA INSURANCE TO RAISE SHARE CAPITAL-REPORT.</title>
<headline>NORDIKA INSURANCE TO RAISE SHARE CAPITAL-REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The shareholders of insurance company Nordika decided to raise the commpany's share capital from 40 to 60 million kroons, Aripaev newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>The share capital will be raised via a bonus share issue, Nordika's chairman Jaanus Reisner was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>Managing director Tiit Arge said the insurance company has no plans to seek a bourse listing as it does not need any additional capital.</p>
<p>Nordika had a net profit of 24.5 million kroons in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
